      "name": "remote-mount",
      "title": "Remote-mount a harness",
      "description": "Bring a harness, and every layer it depends on, into a checkout that does not hold it, from another repository at a pinned commit, as declared directories with a lock: a `source.remote` entry in the downstream's root `index.config.json` (legacy: `remoteMounts` on its declaration) and `mountDefaults` on the harness. Covers when to mount and when to subscribe instead, why there are no submodules and no `.deps/`, the transitive closure through `needs` and gitlinks, overrides by id, the lock, and the three states.",
